       "type": "question",
       "label": null,
       "prompt": "The formula for BMI is $b=\\frac{m}{h^2}$ where $m$ is mass in kilograms and $h$ is height in metres.\n\nMs Nguyen is 165 cm tall and has a BMI of 24.",
       "children": [
        {
         "id": "v2-729c1a-p5-practice-j2-052053-j2-q-a",
         "type": "part",
         "label": "a",
         "prompt": "Use the formula to form an equation in $m$",
         "answerSpaceMm": 25,
         "answer": {
          "short": "$24=\\frac{m}{1.65^2}$",
          "worked": "$165\\text{ cm}=1.65\\text{ m}$\n$$\\begin{align*}b&=\\frac{m}{h^2}\\\\24&=\\frac{m}{1.65^2}\\end{align*}$$"
         }
        },
        {
         "id": "v2-729c1a-p5-practice-j2-052053-j2-q-b",
         "type": "part",
         "label": "b",
         "prompt": "Solve your equation to find her mass.",
         "answerSpaceMm": 30,
         "answer": {
          "short": "$m=65.34\\text{ kg}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}24&=\\frac{m}{1.65^2}\\\\m&=24(1.65^2)\\\\m&=65.34\\end{align*}$$\nHer mass is $65.34\\text{ kg}$."
         }
        }
       ],
